{title: Great Things for Us}
{subtitle: Psalms 126:1–3}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 3/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
When the Lord restored [Ab]the for[Eb]tunes of Zion
We were like [Ab]those [Eb]who dream
Mouths [Ab]filled with [Bb]laughter
[Cm]Tongues [Bb6]with shouts of [Ab]joy
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]The [Bb]Lord has done [Ab]great [Eb]things for us
And [Ab]we are [Bb]glad
[Eb]The [Bb]Lord has done [Ab]great [Eb]things for us
And [Ab]we are [Bb][Eb]glad
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Ab] | [Eb] | [Ab] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Then [Eb]it was said [Bb]a[Ab]mong [Eb]the nations
The Lord [Bb/D]has done [Ab]great things [Eb]for them
Re[Bb/D]store [Ab]our for[Bb]tunes, O [Cm]Lord
[Bb6]Like streams in the [Ab]desert
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]The [Bb]Lord has done [Ab]great [Eb]things for us
And [Ab]we are [Bb]glad
The [Eb]Lord [Bb]has done [Ab]great [Eb]things for us
And [Ab]we are [Bb][Eb]glad
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Ab]Those who sow in [Eb]tears
Will [Bb]reap with shouts of [Cm]joy
Whoev[Ab]er goes out weep[Eb]ing
[Bb]Carrying seed to [Ab]sow
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Will [Eb]come [Bb6]home with [Ab]shouts [Eb]of joy
[Bb/D]Carrying [Ab]the [Eb]sheaves
The Lord [Bb]has done great [Ab]things [Eb]for us
And [Ab]we are [Bb]glad
{end_of_verse}

